diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 531a5cc..ea43cbd 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -119,6 +119,16 @@ macOS currently provides a limited CoreGraphics synthetic-input backend for
 keyboard and mouse only. It is not a virtual-HID backend and does not yet
 support gamepads; native macOS virtual-HID gamepad support is planned.
 
+The ClipRelay macOS host overlay adds `MouseEvent::target` for capture-bound
+CoreGraphics input. Its viewport uses logical desktop points; absolute event
+coordinates retain their capture-pixel extent and fractional precision. Every
+event must carry a target after the mouse has been bound. A newer target version
+releases held buttons at the old target before routing new input. An inactive
+version releases held buttons and cannot be reactivated; use a larger version
+for a new active capture. Closing the mouse also releases only buttons it owns.
+This overlay is applied only to the macOS host build. Other backends do not
+implement capture targets; untargeted macOS callers retain primary-screen mapping.
+
 The library is designed around gamepad use first because remote streaming hosts
 are the first consumer class. Non-gamepad device types are available through the
 same API where the backend exposes them.
